  "id": "COMPOUND:19816 - PROTEIN:6256",
  "verbalization": "Fraxinol is implicated in the regulation of Histone H1.0 through a series of molecular interactions involving Neuropilin-2. The evidence suggests that Fraxinol acts as a target for multiple compounds, including (3S,5S)-1-(4-Hydroxy-3-Methoxyphenyl)Decane-3,5-Diol, (E)-3-(4-Acetoxy-3-Methoxy-Phenyl)-Acrylic Acid, and 3-Hydroxyphenylpyruvic acid, all of which are known to target Neuropilin-2. These compounds are likely modulating the activity of Neuropilin-2, which in turn influences the expression of Histone H1.0. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Fraxinol may interact with Histone H1.0, possibly through the modulation of Neuropilin-2 activity. The evidence supports a direct relationship between Fraxinol and Histone H1.0, mediated via Neuropilin-2, and underscores the role of these compounds in the regulation of chromatin structure.",
